      "intro": "If your loved one is 60+ and facing legal problems with their health coverage, housing, or elder abuse, Maine Legal Services for the Elderly provides free legal help. The program handles Medicare/MaineCare disputes, eviction defense, consumer debt, guardianship issues, and elder abuse protection orders, problems that private attorneys charge hundreds of dollars per hour to resolve.\n\nYour loved one can get immediate advice by calling the helpline at 1-800-750-5353. For complex cases requiring court representation, LSE attorneys are located in offices across Maine. The program prioritizes cases where basic human needs are at stake, so housing emergencies and health coverage denials get faster attention than routine estate planning.",
